<h1>Stampscan Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="text-sm text-gray-400">Effective date: July 16, 2026</p>

<p>
    Stampscan is provided by Euler Soft. This policy explains what Stampscan processes, why it is
    processed, where it is stored, and the choices available to you.
</p>

<h2>Information Stampscan Processes</h2>

<h3>Stamp images and identification requests</h3>
<p>
    When you request an identification, the front and optional back images you capture or explicitly
    select are sent through Stampscan&apos;s Cloudflare Worker to Google Gemini to produce identification
    and valuation results. Euler Soft does not use submitted images to train its own models or for
    advertising. The identify endpoint does not write those images to Stampscan&apos;s persistent cloud
    media storage. Cloudflare and Google may process transient copies and limited operational records
    under their applicable service terms and privacy commitments.
</p>
<p>
    Images saved in your collection are stored on your device in app-owned storage. Stampscan does
    not currently provide user-facing cloud collection synchronization. Local images remain until you
    remove the applicable local data or uninstall the app.
</p>

<h3>Device and app identifiers</h3>
<p>
    Stampscan creates anonymous installation, Worker user, and credit-owner identifiers. They establish
    secure sessions, enforce free-use and paid entitlements, prevent abuse, manage credits, and make
    retries idempotent. Security credentials use protected system storage such as Keychain where
    applicable.
</p>

<h3>Purchases and subscriptions</h3>
<p>
    Apple processes payments. Stampscan and RevenueCat process product identifiers, entitlement and
    subscription status, transaction-related identifiers, and purchase history needed to unlock paid
    features, restore purchases, synchronize entitlement state, and provide support. Stampscan does
    not receive or store payment-card details.
</p>

<h3>Collection information</h3>
<p>
    Stamp records, collection membership, notes, value snapshots, and related images are stored locally
    with Core Data and app-owned file storage. If you explicitly share or export information, iOS sends
    it to the destination you choose.
</p>

<h3>Analytics, attribution, and diagnostics</h3>
<p>
    Stampscan may process app events, coarse device and app information, installation or attribution
    identifiers, subscription state, and crash or performance diagnostics through Firebase Analytics,
    Firebase Crashlytics, RevenueCat, and AppsFlyer. Stamp images, collection contents, and notes are not
    intentionally included in analytics or crash events. AppsFlyer advertising attribution follows your
    App Tracking Transparency choice. Stampscan does not sell personal information.
</p>

<h2>Purposes</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Identify stamps and provide estimated values</li>
    <li>Save and organize a local collection</li>
    <li>Authenticate requests and protect the service</li>
    <li>Apply free-use, credit, and subscription entitlements</li>
    <li>Complete, restore, and support purchases</li>
    <li>Improve reliability, understand feature use, and diagnose crashes</li>
    <li>Measure acquisition when tracking permission allows it</li>
    <li>Prevent fraud and comply with legal obligations</li>
</ul>
<p>
    Identification and valuation results are automated estimates for informational purposes and are not
    professional appraisals.
</p>

<h2>Service Providers</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Cloudflare for Worker execution, security, request handling, and related infrastructure</li>
    <li>Google Gemini for AI-assisted identification and result generation</li>
    <li>Google Firebase for analytics, Remote Config, and crash diagnostics</li>
    <li>RevenueCat for subscription and entitlement management</li>
    <li>AppsFlyer for install attribution and permitted advertising measurement</li>
    <li>Apple for App Store purchases, StoreKit, permissions, and platform services</li>
</ul>
<p>
    These providers process information under their applicable terms, privacy policies, security
    controls, and retention practices. Processing may occur outside your country subject to legally
    required transfer safeguards.
</p>

<h2>Retention and Deletion</h2>
<p>
    Identification images are not persisted by Stampscan&apos;s identify endpoint after request processing.
    Google may retain prompts and responses for a limited period for abuse monitoring under its paid
    Gemini API terms. Locally saved records remain until you remove them or uninstall Stampscan.
    Temporary scan drafts are removed by the app&apos;s cleanup lifecycle.
</p>
<p>
    Anonymous identifiers, credit operations, entitlement records, and limited security metadata may be
    retained as needed to operate entitlements, prevent duplicate charging or abuse, satisfy accounting
    or legal duties, and resolve disputes. Provider-held analytics, diagnostic, attribution, and purchase
    records follow each provider&apos;s configured controls and policies.
</p>
<p>
    You may request access to or deletion of server-side information associated with your installation by
    contacting Euler Soft. Support may request an in-app installation identifier to locate anonymous
    records. Legally required transaction, fraud-prevention, or security records may be retained.
</p>

<h2>Your Choices</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Decline camera, photo-library, notification, or tracking permissions</li>
    <li>Select only the images you want Stampscan to process</li>
    <li>Manage or cancel subscriptions through your Apple ID settings</li>
    <li>Restore purchases in Stampscan</li>
    <li>Remove local collection data or uninstall the app</li>
    <li>Request privacy assistance using the contact below</li>
</ul>

<h2>Security</h2>
<p>
    Stampscan uses encrypted network transport, scoped credentials, protected local storage, request
    authentication, and access controls appropriate to the information. No storage or transmission
    method can guarantee absolute security.
</p>

<h2>Age Requirement</h2>
<p>
    Stampscan and its AI identification service are intended for adults aged 18 or older. Euler Soft does
    not knowingly collect personal information from children. Contact us if you believe a child has
    provided information so it can be reviewed and deleted where appropriate.
</p>

<h2>Policy Changes</h2>
<p>
    This policy may change when features, providers, or legal obligations change. The effective date will
    be updated when material changes are published.
</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>
    For privacy questions or requests, contact
    <a href="mailto:eulersoft@outlook.com">eulersoft@outlook.com</a>.
</p>
